1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,696
Posting on social media
every day can eat your time.

2
00:00:03,696 --> 00:00:07,076
In this lesson, you'll use
the Social Planner to write,

3
00:00:07,076 --> 00:00:11,625
schedule and manage posts for all your
social accounts, from one calendar.

4
00:00:12,478 --> 00:00:15,420
You'll find it under
Marketing, Social Planner.

5
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:18,048
The calendar shows everything at a glance.

6
00:00:18,048 --> 00:00:21,992
Blue posts are scheduled, and
green ones are already published.

7
00:00:21,992 --> 00:00:25,434
The little icons show which
accounts each post goes to.

8
00:00:26,282 --> 00:00:28,175
First, connect your accounts.

9
00:00:28,175 --> 00:00:29,676
Click Connect accounts.

10
00:00:29,676 --> 00:00:34,899
You can link a Facebook page, Instagram,
your Google Business Profile, LinkedIn,

11
00:00:34,899 --> 00:00:35,747
TikTok and X.

12
00:00:35,747 --> 00:00:39,598
Click Connect, log in to that
network once, and you're set.

13
00:00:40,449 --> 00:00:43,225
Switch to Week for a
closer look at timings.

14
00:00:43,225 --> 00:00:47,263
Or switch to List, where you can
filter by scheduled, published,

15
00:00:47,263 --> 00:00:48,778
drafts and failed posts.

16
00:00:48,778 --> 00:00:53,636
Failed is worth checking now and then,
usually it just means an account needs

17
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:54,456
reconnecting.

18
00:00:55,309 --> 00:00:56,710
Now let's create one.

19
00:00:56,710 --> 00:00:57,712
Click New Post.

20
00:00:57,712 --> 00:00:59,914
At the top, choose where it goes.

21
00:00:59,914 --> 00:01:02,850
Facebook and Instagram
are already selected.

22
00:01:02,850 --> 00:01:06,588
Let's add LinkedIn too, so
we reach local professionals.

23
00:01:07,443 --> 00:01:08,501
Stuck for words?

24
00:01:08,501 --> 00:01:11,740
Click Content AI, and
describe the post you want.

25
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:15,112
Here, an invitation to our
Invisalign open evening.

26
00:01:15,112 --> 00:01:20,598
Click Generate, and in seconds you have a
friendly draft, with emojis and hashtags.

27
00:01:20,598 --> 00:01:23,441
Always read it, and
make it sound like you.

28
00:01:24,296 --> 00:01:28,595
Posts with an image get far more
attention, and Instagram needs one.

29
00:01:28,595 --> 00:01:32,198
Click Add media, and pick a
file from your Media Storage.

30
00:01:32,198 --> 00:01:34,727
It appears straight away in the preview.

31
00:01:35,576 --> 00:01:38,579
On the right, preview the
post for each network.

32
00:01:38,579 --> 00:01:42,458
Instagram shows the image first,
with your caption underneath.

33
00:01:42,458 --> 00:01:44,585
LinkedIn looks more like Facebook.

34
00:01:44,585 --> 00:01:48,776
Check each one, because long text
gets cut off in different places.

35
00:01:49,627 --> 00:01:50,822
Don't forget Google.

36
00:01:50,822 --> 00:01:55,724
Posts to your Google Business Profile show
up on your listing in Google Search and

37
00:01:55,724 --> 00:01:58,473
Maps, right where local
customers are looking.

38
00:01:58,473 --> 00:02:02,239
Keep them short, because Google
only shows the first few lines,

39
00:02:02,239 --> 00:02:04,570
and they come with a handy Book button.

40
00:02:05,418 --> 00:02:07,558
Finally, pick when it goes out.

41
00:02:07,558 --> 00:02:13,079
Let's choose Thursday 5 November at 18:00,
when people are scrolling after work.

42
00:02:13,079 --> 00:02:16,392
Click Schedule, and there
it is on the calendar.

43
00:02:16,392 --> 00:02:19,843
You could also post it
now, or save it as a draft.

44
00:02:20,695 --> 00:02:22,738
Some posts are worth repeating.

45
00:02:22,738 --> 00:02:25,506
Our Smile Tip Tuesday goes out every week.

46
00:02:25,506 --> 00:02:30,317
Open it, and you'll see Recurring post
switched on, set to repeat weekly.

47
00:02:30,317 --> 00:02:34,205
It's perfect for evergreen
tips, opening hours and reviews.

48
00:02:35,054 --> 00:02:36,138
Here's a pro tip.

49
00:02:36,138 --> 00:02:40,922
Give each weekday a theme, like tips
on Tuesday and team stories on Friday.

50
00:02:40,922 --> 00:02:44,940
Then set aside one hour a month
to schedule everything at once.

51
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:48,831
You'll post consistently without
thinking about it every day.

52
00:02:49,688 --> 00:02:52,094
Your social media is now on autopilot.

53
00:02:52,094 --> 00:02:56,021
In the last lesson of this module,
you'll learn trigger links,

54
00:02:56,021 --> 00:02:59,187
so you can see exactly who
clicked, and act on it.

55
00:02:59,187 --> 00:03:00,074
See you there.
